<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_AiAgentTaskCostTracking" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Web Modeler" exporterVersion="63e7f30" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:error id="Error_PriceNotFound" name="Price not found" errorCode="PRICE_NOT_FOUND" />
  <!--
    Activity_AiAgentTask is a REAL io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.v1 element (not a
    placeholder), wired to Camunda's provided LLM endpoint (CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_ENDPOINT/
    _API_KEY secrets) calling anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5. Its result variable is "agent".

    Token usage is at agent.context.metrics.tokenUsage.{inputTokenCount, outputTokenCount}
    (plus agent.context.metrics.modelCalls) - read from a real process instance on a live
    cluster (AI Agent element template v7, openaiCompatible provider); it does NOT need "Include
    assistant message". An earlier version of this file, the README and the tests used
    agent.responseMessage.metadata.framework.tokenUsage, which does not exist on that result:
    the Token cost job then failed validation with "inputTokens: must not be null".

    The connector's "Agent name" input is called agentName, NOT agent: the AI Agent Task's default
    result variable is "agent", and an input mapping of the same name shadows it for the token
    mappings that follow it (Zeebe applies input mappings in order, each visible to the next).

    Deliberately a single straight-line pass (Start -> AI Agent Task -> Token cost -> Done), not a
    loop: an earlier version of this file had a "continue looping?" gateway looping back to
    Activity_AiAgentTask, but a real AI Agent Task has no "continueLoop" concept of its own (it
    runs its own internal tool-call loop up to data.limits.maxModelCalls and completes once), so
    that loop-back could never actually fire - continueLoop was always undefined, and Modeler's
    own linter flags a task with multiple incoming sequence flows and no explicit join as an error
    ("Incoming flows do not join") regardless. If you want to chain multiple AI Agent Task
    activations of your own, reintroduce a loop-back edge and gateway explicitly, driven by
    whatever real signal decides to continue - not by this file's old vestigial pattern.

    WHY THE business_ PREFIX: on Camunda 8.10 SaaS clusters the default Optimize data filter exports
    only variables whose names start with "business_". Without the prefix Optimize never sees the
    totals (its report builder shows the Variable view as unavailable) and the variables are never
    back-filled. business_totalCostUsd (USD) / business_totalCost (whole micro-dollars,
    1,000,000 = 1 USD) are the running totals,
    business_costAgent is the agent name of the last Token cost call (a plain string, because
    Optimize does not flatten the tokenCostResult object on SaaS), and business_taskAgentCost is
    this agent's own cost in whole micro-dollars (the same figure as business_totalCost here; it
    exists so Optimize can show a cost tile per agent, next to the sub-process demo's agents).
    business_taskAgentInputTokens / OutputTokens / TotalTokens are this agent's tokens, copied
    from tokenCostResult so Optimize can show them per agent.
    The Prometheus counters and the
    connector's own tokenCostResult are unaffected. See optimize/ai-cost-dashboard.json.

    OPERATIONAL GOTCHA, hit once already: if you re-apply/update the "Token Cost Reporter"
    element template on Activity_TokenCost in Modeler (e.g. after a version bump), Modeler
    regenerates that task's ENTIRE zeebe:ioMapping from the template's own known fields only -
    silently deleting the eight zeebe:output lines below (tokenCostResult, business_totalCost,
    business_totalCostUsd, business_costAgent, business_taskAgentCost and the three
    business_taskAgent...Tokens variables) that aren't part of the template's own field set,
    since they were added by hand. If the totals stop accumulating after touching this task in
    Modeler, this is why - re-add those eight output lines afterward.
  -->
  <bpmn:process id="ai-agent-task-cost-tracking" name="AI Agent Task with token/cost tracking" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_1" name="Start">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=0" target="business_totalCost" />
          <zeebe:output source="=0" target="business_totalCostUsd" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_StartToAgent</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_AiAgentTask" name="AI Agent Task" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.v1" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="7" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.camunda.agenticai:aiagent:1" retries="1" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="openaiCompatible" target="provider.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_ENDPOINT}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.endpoint" />
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.CAMUNDA_PROVIDED_LLM_API_KEY}}" target="provider.openaiCompatible.authentication.apiKey" />
          <zeebe:input source="anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5" target="provider.openaiCompatible.model.model" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;You are **TaskAgent**, a helpful, generic chat agent that can handle a wide variety of customer requests using your own domain knowledge **and** any tools explicitly provided to you at runtime.&#10;&#10;If tools are provided, you should prefer them instead of guessing an answer. You can call the same tool multiple times by providing different input values. Don&#39;t guess any tools which were not explicitly configured. If no tool matches the request, try to generate an answer. If you&#39;re not able to find a good answer, return with a message stating why you&#39;re not able to.&#10;&#10;Wrap minimal, inspectable reasoning in *exactly* this XML template:&#10;&#10;&#60;thinking&#62;&#10;&#60;context&#62;…briefly state the customer’s need and current state…&#60;/context&#62;&#10;&#60;reflection&#62;…list candidate tools, justify which you will call next and why…&#60;/reflection&#62;&#10;&#60;/thinking&#62;&#10;&#10;Reveal **no** additional private reasoning outside these tags.&#34;" target="data.systemPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=&#34;Hello! Please briefly introduce yourself and explain what kind of requests you can help with.&#34;" target="data.userPrompt.prompt" />
          <zeebe:input source="=agent.context" target="data.context" />
          <zeebe:input source="in-process" target="data.memory.storage.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=20" target="data.memory.contextWindowSize" />
          <zeebe:input source="=10" target="data.limits.maxModelCalls" />
          <zeebe:input source="text" target="data.response.format.type" />
          <zeebe:input source="=false" target="data.response.format.parseJson" />
          <zeebe:input source="=true" target="data.response.includeAssistantMessage" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="7" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.camunda.connectors.agenticai.aiagent.v1" />
          <zeebe:header key="resultVariable" value="agent" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT0S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_StartToAgent</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_AgentToTokenCost</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_TokenCost" name="Token cost" zeebe:modelerTemplate="io.github.camunda.TokenCostGovernor.v2" zeebe:modelerTemplateVersion="6" zeebe:modelerTemplateIcon="data:image/svg+xml;base64,">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="io.github.camunda:token-cost-governor:1" retries="1" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="{{secrets.GOVERNOR_PRICE_TABLE}}" target="priceTableSecret" />
          <zeebe:input source="anthropic" target="provider" />
          <zeebe:input source="claude-haiku-4-5" target="model" />
          <zeebe:input source="task-agent" target="agentName" />
          <zeebe:input source="=agent.context.metrics.tokenUsage.inputTokenCount" target="inputTokens" />
          <zeebe:input source="=agent.context.metrics.tokenUsage.outputTokenCount" target="outputTokens" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult" target="tokenCostResult" />
          <zeebe:output source="=business_totalCost + tokenCostResult.costMicros" target="business_totalCost" />
          <zeebe:output source="=business_totalCostUsd + tokenCostResult.costUsd" target="business_totalCostUsd" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult.agent" target="business_costAgent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult.costMicros" target="business_taskAgentCost" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult.inputTokens" target="business_taskAgentInputTokens" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult.outputTokens" target="business_taskAgentOutputTokens" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tokenCostResult.totalTokens" target="business_taskAgentTotalTokens" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
        <zeebe:taskHeaders>
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateVersion" value="6" />
          <zeebe:header key="elementTemplateId" value="io.github.camunda.TokenCostGovernor.v2" />
          <zeebe:header key="resultVariable" value="tokenCostResult" />
          <zeebe:header key="retryBackoff" value="PT0S" />
        </zeebe:taskHeaders>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_AgentToTokenCost</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_TokenCostToDone</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="BoundaryEvent_PriceNotFound" name="PRICE_NOT_FOUND" attachedToRef="Activity_TokenCost">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_BoundaryToLog</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrorEventDefinition_1" errorRef="Error_PriceNotFound" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_LogUnknownModelPrice" name="Log unknown model price">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="demo.log:unknown-model-price:1" retries="1" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_BoundaryToLog</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_LogToEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_TokenCostToDone" sourceRef="Activity_TokenCost" targetRef="EndEvent_Done" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Done" name="Done">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_TokenCostToDone</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_UnknownModelPrice" name="Unknown model price">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_LogToEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_StartToAgent" sourceRef="StartEvent_1" targetRef="Activity_AiAgentTask" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_AgentToTokenCost" sourceRef="Activity_AiAgentTask" targetRef="Activity_TokenCost" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_BoundaryToLog" sourceRef="BoundaryEvent_PriceNotFound" targetRef="Activity_LogUnknownModelPrice" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_LogToEnd" sourceRef="Activity_LogUnknownModelPrice" targetRef="EndEvent_UnknownModelPrice" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="ai-agent-task-cost-tracking">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_1">
        <dc:Bounds x="152" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_AiAgentTask_di" bpmnElement="Activity_AiAgentTask">
        <dc:Bounds x="280" y="200" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_TokenCost_di" bpmnElement="Activity_TokenCost">
        <dc:Bounds x="440" y="200" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_LogUnknownModelPrice_di" bpmnElement="Activity_LogUnknownModelPrice">
        <dc:Bounds x="440" y="360" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Done_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Done">
        <dc:Bounds x="602" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_UnknownModelPrice_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_UnknownModelPrice">
        <dc:Bounds x="602" y="382" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="BoundaryEvent_PriceNotFound_di" bpmnElement="BoundaryEvent_PriceNotFound">
        <dc:Bounds x="472" y="262" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_TokenCostToDone_di" bpmnElement="Flow_TokenCostToDone">
        <di:waypoint x="540" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="602" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_StartToAgent_di" bpmnElement="Flow_StartToAgent">
        <di:waypoint x="188" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="280" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_AgentToTokenCost_di" bpmnElement="Flow_AgentToTokenCost">
        <di:waypoint x="380" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="440" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_BoundaryToLog_di" bpmnElement="Flow_BoundaryToLog">
        <di:waypoint x="490" y="298" />
        <di:waypoint x="490" y="360" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_LogToEnd_di" bpmnElement="Flow_LogToEnd">
        <di:waypoint x="540" y="400" />
        <di:waypoint x="602" y="400" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
